//? Title: Angular and cosine margins with label-free inference
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
ArcFace and CosFace modify only the labelled training target after feature/weight normalization. Analytic boundary plots,independent full Jacobians and full NN1/head execution precede visible two-model Adam fitting,restored seen-class confusion and actual unseen-class retrieval images.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/angular_margin.cpp`.

> The method

Normalize feature rows and bias-free class-weight columns,apply a target-only training margin,and optimize explicit softmax CE. Select checkpoints with plain label-free validation logits,then measure seen-class classification separately from class-disjoint verification and retrieval.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/angular_margin_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/angular_margin_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/angular_margin_concept.tikz > build/angular_margin_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/angular_margin_concept.svg build/angular_margin_concept.dvi > build/angular_margin_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
