> Change only the labelled target

Let x be a unit feature row and w_c a unit classifier column. The plain
logit is \(s\cos\theta_c=sx^Tw_c\). During training,the target logit becomes

$$z_y^{Arc}=s\cos(\theta_y+m),\qquad z_y^{Cos}=s(\cos\theta_y-m).$$
\alttext(ArcFace adds an angle margin before cosine;CosFace subtracts a cosine margin. Other class logits remain plain scaled cosines.)

For c=cos(theta),the exact ArcFace transform is
\(\phi(c)=c\cos m-\sqrt{1-c^2}\sin m\),with derivative
\(\cos m+c\sin m/\sqrt{1-c^2}\). CosFace has derivative one.
The implementation clips ArcFace c by epsilon1e-6 and floors the sine radicand
at epsilon. Its default monotonic tail uses c-m*sin(m) when c<=cos(pi-m).
This is an explicit piecewise teaching choice;outside clipped endpoints,the
target gradient is zero. Non-target derivatives bypass the transform.
The native independent formula oracle checks every target/non-target value
and CE derivative,including endpoints,zero margin and both tail policies.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/angular_margin_transform.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto x = n::linspace(-1, 1, 501);
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  for (bool cosface : {false, true}) {
    m::AngularMarginConfig c;
    c.kind = cosface ? m::AngularMarginKind::kCosFace : m::AngularMarginKind::kArcFace;
    c.margin = cosface ? .2f : .3f;
    c.scale = 1;
    auto cosine = n::stack({x, n::zeros_like(x)}, 1).requires_grad_();
    const auto logits = m::ApplyAngularMargin(cosine, n::zeros({501}, n::DType::Int64), 2, c);
    const auto target = n::select(logits, 1, 0),
               gradient = n::select(n::grad(n::sum(target), {cosine})[0], 1, 0);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(x.to_vector<double>(), target.to_vector<double>(), "target", {37, 99, 235})
        .lines(x.to_vector<double>(), gradient.to_vector<double>(), "derivative",
               {220, 38, 38})
        .title(cosface ? "CosFace target and derivative" : "ArcFace target and derivative")
        .x_label("target cosine before margin")
        .y_label("unscaled target / derivative")
        .y_limits(-1.5, 7.5);
    layout.add(p);
  }
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  layout.size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg("build/angular_margin_transform.svg");
  std::print("ArcFace m.3 and CosFace m.2,scale1;only target column transformed. Piecewise "
             "ArcFace monotonic tail,endpoint clipping and all logit derivatives have "
             "independent native oracles.\n");
}
```
