> A two-class boundary that can be checked by hand

Place unit class directions beta=1 radian apart and move a feature through
angle theta from the target direction. Plain normalized softmax has a
boundary beta/2. ArcFace training requires
\(\cos(\theta+m)>\cos(\beta-\theta)\),so its boundary is
\((\beta-m)/2\). CosFace requires
\(\cos\theta-m>\cos(\beta-\theta)\),giving

$$\theta_*^{Cos}=\frac\beta2-\arcsin\!\left(\frac{m}{2\sin(\beta/2)}\right).$$
\alttext(The cosine margin moves the two-class training boundary toward the target direction by an arcsine displacement.)

Both shrink the target’s accepted training region. These formulas apply on
the illustrated ordinary angular branch,away from the clipped/tail cases.
They describe training;label-free inference retains the plain beta/2 boundary.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/angular_margin_boundary.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  const auto theta = n::linspace(0, 1, 201);
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  for (bool cosface : {false, true}) {
    const double margin = cosface ? .2 : .3,
                 boundary =
                     cosface ? .5 - std::asin(margin / (2 * std::sin(.5))) : (1 - margin) / 2;
    m::AngularMarginConfig c;
    c.kind = cosface ? m::AngularMarginKind::kCosFace : m::AngularMarginKind::kArcFace;
    c.margin = float(margin);
    c.scale = 1;
    const auto cosine = n::stack({n::cos(theta), n::cos(1. - theta)}, 1),
               labels = n::zeros({201}, n::DType::Int64);
    const auto logits = m::ApplyAngularMargin(cosine, labels, 2, c);
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.lines(theta.to_vector<double>(), n::select(logits, 1, 0).to_vector<double>(), "target",
            {37, 99, 235})
        .lines(theta.to_vector<double>(), n::select(logits, 1, 1).to_vector<double>(),
               "competitor", {220, 38, 38})
        .lines({boundary, boundary}, {.2, 1.}, "boundary", {22, 163, 74})
        .title(cosface ? "CosFace training boundary" : "ArcFace training boundary")
        .x_label("feature angle from target;radians")
        .y_label("unscaled class logit")
        .y_limits(.2, 1.25);
    layout.add(p);
    std::print("{} training boundary {:.9f} rad;plain inference boundary.5 rad. Native checks "
               "verify equality and opposite sides.\n",
               cosface ? "CosFace" : "ArcFace", boundary);
  }
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  layout.size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg("build/angular_margin_boundary.svg");
}
